=== greptile-apps[bot] 2026-10-14T12:14:11Z api/routes.py:26753
<a href="#"><img alt="P1" src="https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9" align="top"></a> **Wakeups use another profile's effort**

`_start_run` reads `get_config()` outside the session's profile scope. Automatic process and delegation wakeups run on fresh threads without that scope, and `_server_initiated_turn_routing` restores the previous scope before this read. A named-profile session therefore receives the process profile's reasoning effort instead of its own. For example, a process profile set to `none` disables reasoning for a session whose profile requests `high`.

Resolve the effort and model capabilities inside the owning session's profile scope.

**Knowledge Base Used:**
- [Chat and agent execution](https://app.greptile.com/hermes-webui/-/custom-context/knowledge-base/nesquena/hermes-webui/-/docs/chat-and-agent-execution.md)
- [Configuration and integrations](https://app.greptile.com/hermes-webui/-/custom-context/knowledge-base/nesquena/hermes-webui/-/docs/configuration-and-integrations.md)

