=== greptile-apps[bot] 2026-10-14T13:13:50Z api/gateway_chat.py:375
<a href="#"><img alt="P1" src="https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9" align="top"></a> **`ultra` skips model limits**

When `agent.reasoning_effort` is `ultra`, this early return skips every model-specific limit. For example, `o3-mini` on OpenAI supports at most `high`, but this path sends `ultra` when the receiver advertises it, or `xhigh` otherwise. Both exceed that model's limit and can make the chat fail.

Preserve `ultra` for models that support it, but apply the selected model's limits before checking what the receiver can parse.

=== greptile-apps[bot] 2026-10-14T15:13:12Z api/config.py:12830
<a href="#"><img alt="P1" src="https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9" align="top"></a> **Streaming falsely implies effort support**

`get_gateway_caps()` treats `reasoning_streaming` as proof that the receiver accepts `max` and `ultra`, even without an advertised `reasoning_efforts` list. `_receiver_reasoning_efforts()` makes the same assumption for runners. This violates the repository directive to “fail closed when safety cannot be confirmed: unknown is not allowed.”

If a receiver streams reasoning but only accepts the older effort names, these branches bypass the `xhigh` fallback and send a level the receiver drops. Remove both shortcuts; preserve higher levels only when the receiver explicitly advertises them.

**Context Used:** AGENTS.md ([source](https://github.com/nesquena/hermes-webui/blob/master/AGENTS.md))


